    "title": "Wahine soccer homestand continues on Thursday - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Rob DeMello ,\n1 hours ago The University of Hawaiʻi women’s soccer team continues its homestand this week with the Outrigger No Ka Oi tournament at the Waipiʻo Peninsula Soccer Stadium.\nThe Rainbow Wahine (1-2-1) will face Northern Arizona on Thursday at 7 p.m. before closing the weekend against California Baptist on Sunday at 4 p.m.\nHawaiʻi opened its home slate last week with a split, defeating Central Arkansas 1-0 before falling 3-0 to Oregon. Caroline Carter netted her first career goal in the first half of Thursday’s win, while goalkeepers Kennedy Justin and Brianna Chirpich combined for the shutout as UH outshot the Bears 22-6.\nSunday’s loss to Oregon marked just the Rainbow Wahine’s second home defeat in their last 10 matches dating back to 2024, and the first time this season they were held scoreless.\nUH will now look to regroup behind preseason All-Mountain West picks Amber Gilbert and Nalani Damacion.\nNeither game this week will be televised, but stay with KHON2 Sports on-air and online for continuing coverage.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KHON2.",
